---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import {authoredGuides,guidePath} from '../../lib/authored-guides';
import {getMake} from '../../lib/cars';
---
<Base title="Vehicle-specific diagnostic guides" description="Read diagnostic guides that explain the documented causes, decision points and repair boundaries for a specific vehicle and trouble code." breadcrumbs={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Guides'}]}>
 <div class="container"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">DIAGNOSIS WITH VEHICLE CONTEXT</p><h1>Follow the evidence.</h1><p class="lede">A useful guide explains what would distinguish one cause from another. Start with the vehicle and engine covered by the source.</p></header>
 <section class="section" aria-label="Published diagnostic guides"><div class="model-preview-grid">{authoredGuides.map(guide=><a class="model-preview authored-guide-card" href={guidePath(guide)} data-guide-id={guide.id}><div class="model-preview-top"><span class="eyebrow">{getMake(guide.makeId).name} · {guide.codes.join(' / ')}</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><h2>{guide.title}</h2><p class="model-summary">{guide.description}</p><span class="model-preview-footer">Read the diagnostic guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></a>)}</div>{!authoredGuides.length&&<p class="notice">Vehicle-specific guides will appear here after their source review is complete.</p>}</section>
 <div class="prose guide-library-note"><p>Looking up a definition? The <a href="/codes/">code dictionary</a> lists reference labels separately from these diagnostic guides.</p><p><a href="/tools/">Scan-report checklist</a> · <a href="/safety/">Safety boundaries</a> · <a href="/models/">Documented vehicle cases</a></p></div></div>
</Base>
<style>.authored-guide-card h2{font-size:27px;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.035em}.guide-library-note{margin-bottom:65px}.authored-guide-card{min-width:0}.model-preview-grid{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}@media(max-width:700px){.model-preview-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}</style>
